From: Guohan Lu <securely1g@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Import reviewed APT locks and assemble selected package layers

Carry https://github.com/securely1g/rules_distroless/pull/1 as a patch
to the upstream 0.9.4 release, owned by sonic-build-infra. Keep its existing dependency and tar-tool versions.

SONiC image builders need to retain packages supplied by their base image.
Expose the complete locked package set through a public provider, import
reviewed v2 locks without resolving again, and let flatten accept a checked
ordered subset of declared archives. This removes consumer reliance on
private repository names, generated Bazel lock internals, and a second tar
assembly implementation.

The existing .inc header fix remains in its separate preceding patch.
Tests import an existing Debian package and build only tar archives.

Signed-off-by: Guohan Lu <securely1g@gmail.com>
---
